From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Grok Bot (for Rich)" <hardcopi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:33:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] App mode (ASB_APP): serve one web app such as AmiDiscord
 instead of a browser

New chrome/appmode.inc, off unless ASB_APP is set, so AmiSurf sessions are unchanged.
- ASB_APP id, ASB_APP_URL start page (loaded at start, cmd app home), ASB_APP_TITLE fallback title,
  ASB_APP_ALLOW host globs (default: Discord's hosts + hCaptcha), ASB_APP_EXTERNAL client|deny.
- Top-level documents of the page are checked with Fetch (request stage) before they load; other hosts are
  cancelled and sent to the client as the new ASBC_OPENURL (48, reason 0 link, 1 new window, 2 client NAV).
- New windows (window.open, target=_blank): a second CDP connection to the browser endpoint auto-attaches to new
  pages paused (waitForDebuggerOnStart), catches their first document request, closes them; allowlisted URLs open
  in the app's own page, others go out as OPENURL. Nothing reaches the external site.
- No tabs (TABNEW/TABSEL/TABCLS ignored, no TABS message), no asb:// pages server, no bookmarks/history/suggest,
  no password manager (no probe/autofill/bar), no save page/source/PDF: only zoom, find, ctx, avdelay and
  'app home|reducedmotion 0|1' commands. Client NAV only to allowlisted hosts.
- Reduced motion (ASB_APP_REDUCEDMOTION, default on; cmd app reducedmotion 0|1): prefers-reduced-motion: reduce
  emulated, plus frame throttling: at most one update per ASB_APP_SMALL_MS (100) and changes over a quarter of the
  view at most once per ASB_APP_BIG_MS (1000); held frames are replaced and flushed, so the last state arrives.
  ASB_APP_DARK=1 also emulates prefers-color-scheme: dark.
- ASB_APP_MUTE (default 1): Chrome gets --mute-audio and no audio sink, so the app's own sounds never play.
- spawn_chrome builds its argv as an array (same flags as before for AmiSurf).
